# MindBridge AI Core Rules

- Work only on the current task file under `docs/tasks/`.
- The current task file is the highest-priority requirement.
- Follow `docs/03_API_CONTRACT.yaml` for endpoint and DTO field names.
- Follow `docs/02_DATABASE_MVP.md` for database scope and invariants.
- Follow `docs/01_ARCHITECTURE.md` for module boundaries.
- Preserve the existing frontend design unless the task explicitly requires a UI change.
- Do not invent product requirements.
- Do not invent clinical thresholds.
- Do not invent CBT content.
- Do not invent Safety policy.
- Do not invent data access policy.
- Do not implement diagnosis.
- Do not claim clinical certainty.
- Do not train or fine-tune an AI model.
- Do not introduce Microservices, Kubernetes or unrelated infrastructure.
- Make the smallest complete change that satisfies the current task.
- Do not refactor unrelated modules.
- Reuse current project patterns before creating new abstractions.
- Report conflicts or missing information before changing behavior.
- Never commit secrets, API keys, tokens or passwords.
- Never claim a test passed unless the command was actually executed.
- Report the exact verification command and observed result.
- Update OpenAPI when a shared API contract changes.
- Update implementation status after completing a task.
- Keep code understandable for a two-developer university team.
- Prefer simple and explicit code over generic frameworks.
- Avoid premature abstraction.
- When uncertain, stop and report the uncertainty instead of silently assuming.